      "title": "AAP's Saurabh Bharadwaj seeks FIR over police assault during Delhi protests",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/politics/aap-s-saurabh-bharadwaj-seeks-fir-over-police-assault-during-delhi-protests-126101500385_1.html",
      "description": "Aam Aadmi Party's Delhi unit president Saurabh Bharadwaj on Thursday filed a written complaint to the police commissioner alleging \"life-threatening\" physical assault on him during the recent protests.\nBharadwaj demanded that an FIR be filed for \"criminal conspiracy\" and an independent investigation be conducted into a \"dangerous, life-threatening pattern of physical assault\" on him by Delhi Police and other security forces deployed at the time.\n\"I am writing to file a formal, consolidated complaint regarding three highly severe and dangerous incidents of physical assault inflicted upon me by Delhi Police personnel and paramilitary staff during public gatherings in Delhi. The nature, execution and recurrence of these attacks clearly demonstrate that they are not routine measures for crowd control,\" Bharadwaj said in his letter.\nInstead, they constitute a \"coordinated criminal conspiracy to cause me grievous bodily harm or death under the guise of official duty,\" he added.\nHe furthe",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-15T06:31:16"
    },
    {
      "title": "Delhi Police files FIR against journalist over alleged casteist remarks",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/india-news/delhi-police-files-fir-against-journalist-over-alleged-casteist-remarks-126101401006_1.html",
      "description": "Delhi Police has registered an FIR against an independent journalist and others on a complaint by one of its officers alleging casteist remarks, public humiliation and defamation during a protest near Jantar Mantar earlier this month, officials said on Wednesday.\nThe FIR was registered under relevant provisions of the SC/ST (Prevention of Atrocities) Act and sections 221 (Obstructing public servant in discharge of public functions), 356(2) (Defamation) and 3(5) (Common intention) of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita (BNS) based on the complaint by Assistant Commissioner of Police (ACP) Vivek Bhagat, posted in Connaught Place sub-division of New Delhi district.\nEarlier, the independent journalist had alleged sexual assault charges against the ACP and an enquiry of her complaint is being investigated by the Crime Branch of Delhi Police.\nAccording to the FIR, Bhagat was performing law-and-order duty at Jantar Mantar on October 3 when he allegedly overheard the journalist making derogatory ..",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-15T04:09:47"
